---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & cookies"
  description="How TV Tattler uses cookies, advertising and your email — and the choices you have."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header class="page__header">
      <p class="mono page__kicker">Privacy &amp; cookies</p>
      <h1>Your privacy on TV Tattler</h1>
      <p class="page__standfirst">
        This page explains, in plain English, what data TV Tattler collects, why,
        and the choices you have. We keep it to the minimum needed to run the site.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="page__body">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        TV Tattler is an independent UK entertainment site covering soaps, telly and
        film. For any privacy question, contact
        <a href="mailto:editor@tvtattler.com">editor@tvtattler.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        TV Tattler is free to read because it carries advertising. We use Google
        AdSense to serve ads. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads
        based on your visits to this and other sites.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use <strong>Google Consent Mode</strong>: when you first visit, advertising
        and analytics cookies are set to <em>denied</em> until you make a choice in
        our cookie banner. Choose <strong>Accept</strong> to allow personalised ads,
        or <strong>Reject</strong> to see only non-personalised ads. You can change
        your mind any time by clearing this site’s data in your browser, which brings
        the banner back.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="external nofollow"
          >policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a
        >, and opt out of personalised advertising at
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="external nofollow"
          >google.com/settings/ads</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you sign up for our email newsletter, we store the email address you give
        us so we can send you the newsletter. It is handled by our email provider
        (Mailchimp) purely for that purpose. Every email includes an unsubscribe link,
        and unsubscribing removes you from the list. We never sell or share your
        address.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don’t do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don’t ask you to create an account to read the site.</li>
        <li>We don’t sell your personal data.</li>
        <li>
          We don’t collect more than we need — reading TV Tattler requires no personal
          information at all.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK GDPR you can ask us what data we hold about you, ask us to correct or
        delete it, and object to processing. Email
        <a href="mailto:editor@tvtattler.com">editor@tvtattler.com</a> and we’ll help.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will always live here. Last
        updated August 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
